      "content": "i've been looking at transcripts from the last three G7 summits and there is a really weird pattern with how certain adjectives are used. specifically whenever they talk about 'stability' or 'infrastructure' there's this hyper-specific, almost rhythmic repetition of these otherwise filler words. it feels way too synchronized to be just coincidence. can you look at this snippet and tell me if there's a non-standard structural pattern happening here? like, does the syntax seem artificially constructed?\n\n[TRANSCRIPT SNIPPET: \"...seeking global stability through robust infrastructure. as we stabilize the landscape, we ensure the infrastructure of our shared future remains stable. it is our duty to stabilize these foundations...\"]",
